{:id "0043-lab-learn"
 :title "Lab learn: a style learned from flicks (an optometrist's exam for motion), with a simulation to measure it"
 :lupa/deps #{"0041-lab-stage-flash-test"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :low
 :goal "docs/product/score.md: people will not tune parameters, so a
        style is a point in a four-axis space (:ha/style-point) that moves
        when the writer flicks toward the one of two performances they
        prefer: 'better like this, or like this?'. Build the pure learner
        and a simulation that measures how many flicks it takes
        (hypothesis H5 in docs/product/lab-notebook.md). No UI here."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/learn.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/learn_test.cljc"]
 :design "halfahead.lab.learn (.cljc, pure, the same on both hosts).
          Axes, in this order: :energy :flourish :softness :warmth.
          State: {:point :ha/style-point  ; the current best guess
                  :step {axis s}          ; the size of the next move
                  :dir {axis +1|-1}       ; which way the next move goes
                  :missed {axis n}        ; rejections in a row at this step
                  :axis k                 ; the axis asked about next
                  :flicks n}              ; choices made so far
          (start) and (start point) -> a state at the centre (0.5 on every
            axis) or at point: step 0.25, dir +1, missed 0, axis :energy,
            flicks 0.
          (pair state) -> {:axis k :a point :b point}: :a is the current
            point, :b the point moved by dir * step along the axis, kept
            inside [0 1]; if that leaves :b equal to :a (at a wall), the
            other direction is used. :a and :b always differ.
          (choose state choice) -> the next state, choice :a or :b for the
            pair (pair state) gave. :b: the point becomes :b, the
            direction stays, missed 0. :a: the direction flips, missed + 1,
            and when both directions have now been rejected at this step
            (missed 2) the step halves (never below 1/64) and missed
            returns to 0. Either way :flicks + 1 and :axis moves to the
            next axis, round robin. The point never leaves [0 1] on any
            axis and is always a valid :ha/style-point.
          (distance p q) -> the root mean square difference over the four
            axes.
          A deterministic random source for the simulation, the same on
          both hosts (a small linear congruential generator on integers
          below 2^31; no host randomness).
          (simulate {:hidden point :noise u :flicks n :seed s}) -> a
            vector of n + 1 distances from the learner's point to :hidden,
            before any flick and after each: a simulated reader picks the
            option of each pair nearer to :hidden (by distance), and with
            probability :noise picks the other instead.
          (experiment {:readers r :flicks n :noise u :seed s}) ->
            {:median [..] :p80 [..]}, each n + 1 long: over r readers with
            hidden points drawn uniformly from the unit cube, the median
            and 80th percentile of the distance at each flick count.
          Tests: start and pair shapes; a wall flips the direction; a
          scripted sequence of choices gives the expected point and steps;
          the point stays valid for any sequence of choices (property);
          with no noise a simulated reader's distance never increases
          (property over hidden points); simulate and experiment are
          deterministic for a seed and differ between seeds; and two
          measured facts, asserted loosely so the test is not a coin toss:
          over 300 readers, with no noise the median distance after 24
          flicks is under 0.1, and with noise 0.1 the median after 24
          flicks is below the median before any flick. These two numbers
          are hypotheses, not requirements on the algorithm: if the
          learner as specified misses one, do not tune it to pass; assert
          the value you measured (rounded up to two decimals) instead and
          say so at the top of the final message."
 :acceptance
 ["learn tests as in the design, on both hosts"
  "The final message reports the measured curves, for the foreman's lab
   notebook: (experiment {:readers 1000 :flicks 32 :noise 0.0 :seed 1})
   and the same with :noise 0.1 and 0.25: the median and p80 at 0, 4, 8,
   12, 16, 24 and 32 flicks, to three decimals"
  "`bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["No UI and no changes outside the two files; do not edit the schema"
  "No mapping from a point to motion parameters (another order)"
  "Do not run `bb e2e`, `bb play` or `bb lab:e2e`"]
 :context ["docs/product/score.md" "docs/product/lab-notebook.md"
           "src/halfahead/schema.cljc" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 6.0}
